Census the parallel implementations on the forward-solve accuracy path, so the lead can see whether a weaker duplicate is setting an accuracy floor that the converged-forward-solve plan is not fixing. Context: the resolution-strategy decision of 2026-10-10 and the moment-kernel-repair decision of 2026-10-11 on docs/plans/converged-forward-solve.html; the resolution-pivot reports under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/resolution-pivot/; the evidence fragments under docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/.

Done when the report at the assigned path carries one section per capability below.

Capabilities:
(1) flux and field evaluation at points: analytic kernel point jet, mesh or spline interpolation, sampled raster;
(2) null finding: axis and X-points;
(3) boundary and separatrix extraction;
(4) plasma support and membership: spline clip, exact clip, chord, centroid rule, quadratic fragments, analytic support;
(5) current booking: clipped_support_current_moments, linear and point moments, current.book;
(6) coupling kernels: the packed polygon analytic moments, the executor, the filament kernels, the graded quadrature;
(7) the Grad-Shafranov map: ForwardFluxOperator.flux_map, traced_flux_map, moment.py flux_map, forward.py flux_map, gs.apply;
(8) the exterior field: coils, the certificate's prescribed exterior;
(9) the fixed-point and Newton solvers: newton_krylov, picard, reduced_newton, anderson, the chord route;
(10) profile and source evaluation.

Each section gives:
(a) every implementation in nova/, benchmarks/ and scripts/, and in ~/Code/imas-ambix where it duplicates nova, each as path:line;
(b) which one the production forward solve actually calls, and which the certificate fixture calls, traced as a call chain from forward.py and from scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/measure.py;
(c) the accuracy evidence for each implementation, cited from a receipt, fragment or test with its number, or marked unmeasured;
(d) a verdict:
- clean: one implementation on the production path, and it is the most accurate available;
- floor risk: production calls a path measured or plausibly weaker than another existing one;
- duplicate without floor: parallel copies of equal accuracy.

The report ends with a ranked list of floor risks, each with the measurement that would confirm or clear it and whether an existing plan followup already owns it, naming the followup id.

Read only: change no file outside the report path. Search named subtrees, never a repository root. Cite every claim as a path:line you opened or a receipt you read.

